desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Avoid Yum Update"
	title_zh: "Avoid Yum Update"
	type: audit
	level: low
	rule_id: "source-best-practice-avoid-yum-update"
	risk: "best-practice"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `avoid-yum-update` (dockerfile/best-practice/avoid-yum-update.yaml).
Original message: Packages in base images should be up-to-date, removing the need for 'yum update'. If packages are out-of-date, consider contacting the base image maintainer.
References:
- https://github.com/hadolint/hadolint/wiki/DL3031
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://Dockerfile": <<<POS
yum update
POS
	"safefile://Dockerfile": <<<NEG
yum install
NEG
)

${Dockerfile}.pattern_regex(/(?:yum\s+update)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "low",
	title: "Avoid Yum Update",
	title_zh: "Avoid Yum Update",
	message: "Avoid Yum Update detected.",
}
